    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Onondaga County",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S6464\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act authorizing the county of Onondaga to enter into a lease with\nthe Syracuse Chargers Rowing Club\n\n\n PURPOSE :\nTo authorize a 25-year lease of approximately 1.6 + 1- acres of public\npark property between the County of Onondaga and the Syracuse Chargers\nRowing Club.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\nSection 1 - Notwithstanding any other provision of law, the county of\nOnondaga is authorized to enter into a lease for the period of\ntwenty-five years, for approximately 1.6 acres of public park\nproperty, known as Onondaga Lake Park, with the Syracuse Chargers\nRowing Club for the purpose of conducting rowing activities. The\nSyracuse Chargers Rowing Club shall pay rent in the amount of $2,500\nper year plus utilities, with a five percent increase every five\nyears. A survey depicting such land is on file with the Onondaga\nCounty Clerk's Office.\n\nSection 2 - This act shall take effect immediately.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nCurrently, the County of Onondaga is the owner of certain real\nproperty known as Onondaga Lake Park. Since 1972 a portion of this\nreal property has been used by the Syracuse Chargers Rowing Club by\npermit for the purpose of conducting rowing activities on Onondaga\nLake. This bill was introduced at the request of the Syracuse Chargers\nRowing Club.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nNew.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nUndetermined.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
